From 71a11a405bdba43ed56521222c140692bb3bc6e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: airidosas252 <airidaslideikis@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 14:06:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] tu: traverse the BVH with ray_stack on a8xx

Follow the stock driver: one ray_stack step per visited node replaces
the software stack, its watermark and parent pointer fallback, and the
instance top/bottom bookkeeping. Leaves with primitives left are
intersected again and instances are entered without a step, the step
after an instance entry carries the enter bit. The step result is kept
in current_node and its done/top level bits are handled at the top of
the loop, so a candidate returned to the app keeps its object space
ray. The query's initialization resets the state.

There is one state block per shader, so it's used for the traversals
of ray tracing pipelines, which never interleave, and for shaders with
a single ray query outside ray tracing stages. Everything else, and
A7xx, keeps the software stack, built exactly as before.
